// Title: Potential RipZip Attack on Startup Folder
// Sigma ID: a6976974-ea6f-4e97-818e-ea08625c52cb
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Greg (rule)
// Date: 2022-07-21 | Modified: 2023-01-05
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547
// Description: Detects a phishing attack which expands a ZIP file containing a malicious shortcut. If the
//   victim expands the ZIP file via the explorer process, then the explorer process expands the
//   malicious ZIP file and drops a malicious shortcut redirected to a backdoor into the Startup
//   folder. Additionally, the file name of the malicious shortcut in Startup folder contains
//   {0AFACED1-E828-11D1-9187-B532F1E9575D} meaning the folder shortcut operation.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/jonasLyk/status/1549338335243534336?t=CrmPocBGLbDyE4p6zTX1cg&s=19
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_ripzip_attack.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\Startup" and FolderPath contains ".lnk.{0AFACED1-E828-11D1-9187-B532F1E9575D}") and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\explorer.exe"
